<h2>Exercises for Practice</h2>

<ol>
    <li>
        <strong>Explore</strong>: Use the quadratic explorer above. Set \( a = -1 \), \( b = 0 \), \( c = 4 \).
        Where is the vertex? Is it a maximum or minimum?
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Coding</strong>: Modify the Python code to plot \( f(x) = e^{-x} \sin(x) \) from 0 to 10.
        What do you observe about the amplitude?
    </li>
    <li>
        <strong>Think</strong>: Why does \( x^3 \) grow faster than \( x^2 \) far from the origin, but slower near \( x = 0 \)?
    </li>
</ol>

